# Demon's Crest: title -> new game -> intro -> first playable stage segment.
#
# No-input attract reaches the title screen at ~frame 24000. One Start starts
# a new game (the story intro, $8D = 0xA0 + room). The intro runs ~20000
# frames of cutscene rooms; the first playable stage segment (area 2, the
# graveyard where Firebrand lands) begins around frame 44000. `until` anchors
# the route to the game state instead of the frame count, so a change in
# intro timing cannot silently walk the route off its target.
#
# Used by the widescreen work to prove the gameplay gate ($8D in 1..0x7F)
# and to capture coverage for the stage engine:
#   SNESRECOMP_TIER2_CAPTURE=1 SNESRECOMP_COVERAGE_DIR=coverage/gameplay \
#   ./build/DemonsCrestSNESRecomp "<rom>" --script scripts/routes/gameplay.script
#
# `turbo on` changes presentation pacing only (no guest frames are added), so
# traces and captures are identical to a normal-paced run. The dump lands on
# the first frame the stage engine owns; set SNESRECOMP_DUMP_DIR to collect it.
turbo on
wait 24000
press start 4
until 008D == 02 60000
dump stage_start
wait 600
dump stage_600
quit
